    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d497">

                <pb facs="0411" n="403" xml:id="pg403"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1115/2227a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Consul General at Canton</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Linnell</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-12-16T18:00:00-05:00">December 16, 1937—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>In view of indications that increased Japanese military activity may occur in the
                    Canton area, the Department assumes that you are continuing to impress upon
                    American citizens the advisability of withdrawing while means of egress are
                    available.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
